  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the circuit shown in the figure, there are two parallel plate capacitors each of capacitance <em>C</em>. The switch <em>S<sub>1</sub></em> is pressed first to fully charge the capacitor <em>C<sub>1</sub></em> and the released. The switch <em>S<sub>2</sub></em> is then pressed to charge the capacitor <em>C</em><sub>2</sub>. After some time, <em>S<sub>2</sub></em> is released and then is<em> S<sub>3</sub></em> pressed. After some time,<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/EM00012549_JEE_ADVANCED_2013.jpg\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gfGMW",
      "text": "the charge on the upper plate of C<sub>1</sub> is 2CV<sub>0&nbsp;</sub>.&nbsp;",
